      "id": "tb-14134317afd8f7893989aea5ef545cb8-0001",
      "blockid": "af4d9d05068818630f9dc5c5aa63305a",
      "heading": "E. Operator Selection Based on D3QN",
      "parent_headings": [
        "A Hybrid Metaheuristic Algorithm for Multiobjective Scheduling in Distributed Heterogeneous Flexible Job Shops"
      ],
      "dimension": [
        4,
        2
      ],
      "format": "html",
      "content": "<table><tr><td>Operator Types</td><td>Operator Designs</td></tr><tr><td>Classical operators</td><td>Randomly select two operations, swap their positions. Randomly select one operation and insert it at a specified position. Randomly select two operations, insert one operation before another. Randomly select two operations, insert one operation after another.</td></tr><tr><td>Disruptive and reconstructive operators</td><td>Randomly generate a binary array (0–1), retain positions with 1, randomly redistribute positions with 0. Randomly select a point, maintain positions to the right, shuffle positions to the left. Randomly select a point, maintain positions to the left, shuffle positions to the right. Randomly select two points, disrupt operations between the two points.</td></tr><tr><td>Critical path operators</td><td>Randomly select an operation on the critical path, randomly move all operations of its job to another factory. Randomly select an operation on the critical path, use a roulette wheel selection method to choose a processing factory, move all operations of its job to the selected factory. Randomly select an operation on the critical path, randomly reselect a machining center within its available range. Randomly select an operation on the critical path, use a roulette wheel selection method to choose a machining center, move the current operation to the selected machine for processing.</td></tr></table>",
      "caption": "TABLE IHEURISTIC OPERATOR DESIGN",
      "footnotes": [],
      "self_ref": "content_list.json#/128"
    },
